BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meet + Greet: Hilo: The Hiloday Special by Judd Winick
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T153000
UID:261027ilcv4P-Qe0S6l9Gff7h-Ng
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special meet-and-greet event with Judd Winick\, 
 author of Hilo: The Hiloday Special. This event is free\, but we appreciat
 e your RSVP below so we can plan for your attendance. ABOUT THE BOOK From 
 the New York Times bestselling graphic novel series Hilo comes the first-e
 ver Holiday Special! Hilo and friends are ready for holiday fun\, until a 
 giant\, super-grumpy snowman crashes the celebration. Can they figure out 
 what he wants before the big holiday party? “A story that can be enjoyed
  by the entire family.”—The New York Times “An action-packed page-tu
 rner with heart!” – Dav Pilkey\, creator of DOG MAN The decorations ar
 e up! The gifts are wrapped! And Hilo and the gang are enjoying some holid
 ay togetherness. Sure\, it would be better if the skating pond wasn’t bl
 ocked off. And if someone wasn’t stealing trees from the tree lot. AND i
 f a giant\, super grumpy snowman wasn’t going around destroying things. 
 But what’s a holiday without holiday surprises?! Can Hilo and friends fi
 gure out what the snowman wants before D.J.’s big family party?! Packed 
 with family and food\, love and laughter \\(lots of laughter!\\)—gather 
 around and enjoy all the gifts of the season with Hilo! ABOUT THE AUTHOR J
 udd Winick is the creator of the beloved New York Times bestselling HILO s
 eries\, and the spinoff graphic novel THE MIGHTY. He lives in San Francisc
 o with his wife and their two kids. Judd has written bestselling comic boo
 k series\, has appeared as a cast member on MTV's The Real World: San Fran
 cisco\, and is the author of the acclaimed graphic novel Pedro and Me\, ab
 out his Real World friend AIDS activist Pedro Zamora.
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/983276331451381/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bachata Beginners Thursday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T193000
UID:260317WuAedvrUQkeZCjonoP34uw
DESCRIPTION:Your First Steps into Bachata\n\nThis class is perfect for bac
 hata beginners that want to learn basic steps and skills\, or those who wa
 nt to refresh their foundational skills. We understand that learning somet
 hing new can feel a little intimidating. That’s why our supportive and r
 elaxed environment is specifically designed to make learning bachata basic
 s an absolute blast!\n\nOur friendly instructors will guide you through:\n
 \n**Basic directional steps:** You’ll learn the fundamental movements t
 hat form the building blocks of all bachata dancing.\n\n**Proper frame for
  partner work:** Discover how to connect comfortably and effectively with
  a partner\, setting you up for smooth and enjoyable dances.\n\n**Simple t
 urn patterns:** We’ll introduce you to easy-to-follow turn patterns tha
 t will have you dancing with a partner in no time.\n\nWe’ve carefully or
 ganized our curriculum to ensure that each movement is easy to grasp and r
 emember\, building your confidence with every step. Our goal is to make le
 arning fun. Join us to learn Bachata in Marin.\n\nImportant Details\n\n**N
 o dance experience required:** Whether you’ve never danced before or it
 ’s been a while\, you’re welcome here!\n\n**No partner necessary:** C
 ome solo or bring a friend—either way\, you’ll have plenty of opportun
 ities to dance.\n\nPlease wear **non-marking shoe soles:** This helps us
  keep our dance floor in great condition.\n\nCome join us and discover the
  joy of bachata! We can’t wait to see you on the dance floor.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/bachata-beginners/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
