BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Country Marine Corps Birthday Ball
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T220000
UID:261031kLO2XnVppkm9U8w2gxlQVA
DESCRIPTION:Brigadier General Andrew T. Priddy\, Commanding General of the
  1st Marine Division\, based at Camp Pendleton in Southern California\, wi
 ll be Guest of Honor at Wine Country Marines’ 2026 Marine Corps Birthday
  Ball. The November 7 event at Jacuzzi Family Vineyards will celebrate the
  Corps’ 251st birthday.\n\nSonoma Valley’s annual event began in 1985.
  A formal Marine Corps Birthday Ball is an unusual gathering for a communi
 ty as small as Sonoma\, and its setting in the heart of California Wine Co
 untry has helped it become known as a “Destination Ball\,” drawing Mar
 ines from across the country.\n\nThe local event is part of the worldwide 
 Marine Corps Birthday Ball tradition honoring the Corps’ founding on Nov
 ember 10\, 1775. Marines gather around that date each year to celebrate th
 eir shared history and service.\n\nA career infantry officer and 1995 U.S.
  Naval Academy graduate\, Priddy assumed command of the division in May 20
 26. His participation continues Sonoma Valley’s history of welcoming dis
 tinguished military guests.\n\nFounded by local Marines and their supporte
 rs\, the Sonoma Valley event brings generations together around an endurin
 g conviction: “Once a Marine. Always a Marine.” The evening reflects a
  lifelong commitment to fellow Marines and the community that welcomes the
 m.\n\nThe celebration supports Wine Country Marines’ work assisting serv
 ice members\, veterans and their families through hardship. Military famil
 ies\, veterans and friends of the Corps are invited to join the November 7
  gathering. Explore tickets and reservations at WineCountryMarines.org.
LOCATION:Jacuzzi Family Vineyards
URL:http://WineCountryMarines.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kids Upcycle Clothing and Accessories Event
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T160000
UID:261029Fb7tRIfgakCiXGbKIAOXBg
DESCRIPTION:The parents of children at St. Paul's Episcopal Church in Heal
 dsburg are sponsoring an Upcycle Clothing Event at the church parish hall 
 on Saturday\, Nov. 7\, from 12-4 p.m. Everyone is invited to come by the h
 all at 209 Matheson Street\, grab a grocery-size bag\, pay a fee of $20 an
 d fill the bag with all the clothing\, shoes\, books\, toys and other chil
 dren's items it will hold. All of the items are gently-used and have been 
 collected and sorted by the parents of the kids who attend St. Paul's. Mos
 t items are gently used but some are practically new and have simply been 
 outgrown. A few particularly dressy items will be separately priced. Proce
 eds from the sale will be used to fund children's activities at the church
 \, such as buying art supplies for the newly-refurbished Sunday School roo
 m. That room will be open during the sale for children to visit while thei
 r parents shop. Members of the Episcopal Church Women will assist with the
  sale.
LOCATION:St. Paul's Episcopal Church parish hall
URL:http://www.stpauls-healdsburg.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Park Admission for Veterans and Active Military
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T170000
UID:261028mFU4cfctVkerS4IhN1EYuA
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of their service to the United States\, Jack Lo
 ndon State Historic Park will provide free admission to all active-duty mi
 litary and veterans on Nov. 7\, 8\, 9\, 10\, and 11 - Veterans Day – 202
 6.\n\nBlending the fascinating history of one of America’s most prolific
  and successful writers with the serenity of nature\, Jack London State Hi
 storic Park offers more than 29 miles of back-country trails that roam thr
 ough mixed forests\, redwood groves\, oak woodlands\, and grassy meadows i
 n Sonoma County’s Valley of the Moon.  \n\nActive duty or retired mili
 tary identification or form DD214 can be presented at the entry kiosk to r
 eceive free admission.\n\nAdmission\, regularly priced at $15\, covers one
  vehicle of up to nine passengers for the day.  Park hours are 9 a.m. to 
 5 p.m. daily.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park - Oak Grove Picnic Area (standing
  capacity)
URL:http://www.jacklondonpark.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
