BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Senderos: Los Wappo en Wilikos
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T104500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T130000
UID:261026TfAPDQioQ028Cvk36wFiHQ
DESCRIPTION:\\[Translated to English below\\] Aprende acerca de las histor
 ias y tradiciones de la tribu Wappo\, una de las tribus originarias de est
 a área\, en esta caminata familiar de 2 millas. Nos reuniremos en el esta
 cionamiento del granero blanco \\(el White Barn\\) y caminaremos el sender
 o Meadow mientras escuchamos acerca de la historia cultural de los Wappo e
 n una de sus aldeas ancestral\, Wilikos\, hoy en día parte de Sugarloaf.
  \n\nEvento gratuito\; requiere registración. Hay transportación dispon
 ible gratuita dentro de un radio de 20 millas al parque para familias que 
 la necesiten. Para detalles y registración\, visita EVENT LINK\n\nAlterna
 tivamente\, llama a Mario \\(707-387-4087\\)\, Alma \\(707-247-5767\\)\, e
 ntre martes y sábado\\) o escríbenos a senderos@sonomaecologycenter.org.
  ¿No puedes acompañarnos ese día? ¡Guarda la fecha el 5 de diciembre p
 ara más aventuras!\n\nSenderos Naturales es parcialmente respaldado por u
 na beca de Parks California.\n\nFotografía cortesía de Alma Shaw\n\n\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nLearn about the history and traditions of the M
 ishewal Wappo Tribe\, one of the original groups to live in this area. On 
 this family hike\, will walk approximately 2 miles along the Meadow trail 
 while we listen to the cultural history of the Wappo peoples in one of the
 ir ancestral villages called Wilikios\, today found in Sugarloaf.\n\nThis 
 event is planned around a primarily Latino audience and will be conducted 
 in Spanish. Families from underrepresented groups are welcome to join. Fre
 e transportation available within a 20 mile radius of the park for familie
 s in need. For questions\, please email senderos@sonomaecologycenter.org.\
 n\nThis event is partially supported by Route to Parks\, a project of Park
 s California.\n\nPhoto courtesy of Alma Shaw
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/loswappo26
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mary Collins School at Cherry Valley Presents Beetlejuice JR
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T210000
UID:261026SSd5iLl9z0-R9i_ft0HXEw
DESCRIPTION:Something strange and unusual is coming to Mary Collins at Che
 rry Valley School! The school's Theater Arts Program \\(TAP\\) presents Be
 etlejuice JR.\, running October 30–November 8\, 2026\, featuring two cas
 ts of talented young performers and a student technical crew bringing the 
 beloved Broadway musical to life.\n\nUnder the leadership of Darby Ciampi\
 , Lindsey Nettleton\, and an experienced creative team\, TAP delivers an a
 mbitious theatrical experience that goes far beyond the stage. Students ar
 e involved in every aspect of production\, from acting\, singing\, and cho
 reography to lighting\, sound\, set construction\, costumes\, and props. W
 ith professional mentorship\, students gain hands-on experience in the ful
 l theatrical process\, developing creativity\, confidence\, and collaborat
 ion along the way.
LOCATION:Mary Collins School at Cherry Vallet
URL:https://my.cheddarup.com/c/mccv-beetlejuice-jr/items
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:We Players: Mountain Goddess Ceremony at Western Hills Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T180000
UID:261026HFAmeb1PUUSYp3o50qesfQ
DESCRIPTION:Step into the Garden for an immersive ceremony of release\, re
 newal\, and connection to past\, present\, and future.\n\nConceived and di
 rected by Ava Roy and created and performed by Ling Ling Lee\, *Mountain G
 oddess* invites participants into a sensory journey through Western Hills 
 Garden. Guided by the Mountain Goddess and her spirited guardians\, Ox Hea
 d and Horse Face\, guests will move through meditation\, exploration\, rit
 ual\, and play—drawing on ancestry\, memory\, the elements\, and the lan
 dscape itself.\n\nThe experience culminates in a seasonal\, culturally rel
 evant meal prepared by acclaimed Sonoma County Chef Sean Quan\, featuring
  Beijing Zhajiangmian-style noodle bar with an array of different vegetabl
 es\, pickle\, and herb garnishes. Wine\, beer\, non-alcoholic drinks\, and
  cheerful company will also be provided.\n\nPresented by We Players in pa
 rtnership with Western Hills Garden.\n\n**Conceived and Directed by Ava Ro
 y** **Created and Performed by Ling Ling Lee** **Costumes by Brooke Jennin
 gs**\n\nSliding-scale tickets: $100-200 via We Players website.\n\nArtist 
 Bios:\n\n**Ava Roy**: Ava is the Founding Artistic Director of We Players\
 , the Bay Area site-integrated theater company she founded in 2000. For mo
 re than two decades\, she has created immersive performances that bring au
 diences into new relationships with landscape\, history\, and place\, incl
 uding collaborations with the National Park Service\, California State Par
 ks\, and San Francisco Recreation and Parks. Roy is a graduate of Stanford
  University\, where she designed her own major\, Ritual and Performance in
  Aesthetic Education.\n\n**Ling Ling Lee**: Ling Ling is a San Francisco-b
 orn multidisciplinary artist with a background in Chinese theater and danc
 e. A graduate of San Francisco School of the Arts and Shanghai Theatre Aca
 demy\, Lee works across theater\, dance\, storytelling\, and fire performa
 nce. Her collaborators include We Players\, Meow Wolf\, Disney\, Kaimera W
 anderbeasts\, and the European Juggling Convention. With We Players\, Lee 
 has performed as Ox Head/Horse Face in *Psychopomp* and appeared in *Macbe
 th at Fort Point* and *Odyssea*.\n\n**Brooke Jennings**: **Brooke is an aw
 ard-winning costume designer working in the Bay Area and beyond and a grad
 uate of UC Santa Cruz’s Theater Arts master’s program. Her credits inc
 lude work with San Francisco Playhouse\, Shotgun Players\, San Jose Stage\
 , Crowded Fire Theater Company\, and We Players. Jennings began designing 
 for We Players in 2015 with *Ondine at Sutro*\, for which she received a T
 heater Bay Area Award for Outstanding Costume Design\, and has since becom
 e the company’s resident costume designer and a longtime creative collab
 orator.**
LOCATION:Western Hills Garden
URL:https://www.westernhillsgarden.com/programs/we-players-mountain-goddes
 s-2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
