BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Found Poets! with headliner Jaz Sufi
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T180000
UID:2610142J1MfMg2P0ayh8PPSJVMYA
DESCRIPTION:San Ramon’s Poet Laureate Jaz Sufi filters her slam-honed in
 tensity through queer Iranian-American identity to spin you with spellbind
 ing storytelling.\n\nFound Poets! is about the entertainment of the spirit
  through performance poetry. From our development program grads to nationa
 lly acclaimed headliners\, Found Poets! is a challenging\, committed poetr
 y community dedicated to hosting a good night out.\n\n\\(Headliner\\)\n\nJ
 az Sufi\n\nJaz Sufi \\(she/hers\\) is a queer Iranian-American poet and ar
 ts educator. She is the author of Catalog of Shadows \\(Game Over Books\\)
 . Her work has been published in Best New Poets\, Best of the Net\, AGNI\,
  Black Warrior Review\, Muzzle\, and elsewhere. She is a National Poetry S
 lam finalist and has received fellowships from Kundiman\, the Watering Hol
 e\, and New York University\, where she received her MFA. She is the curre
 nt Poet Laureate of San Ramon on occupied Ohlone land\, where she lives wi
 th her dog\, Apollo. IG: @calamityjaz www.jazsufi.com\n\n\\(Openers\\)\n\n
 Grayson Thompson\n\nGrayson Thompson \\[he/him\\]\, a Black\, Jamaican-Ame
 rican\, queer transgender poet and therapist\, won Foglifter Press’s 202
 4 Start A Riot! Chapbook Prize \\(June 2025\\) and Write Bloody Publishing
 ’s 2024 Jack McCarthy Book Prize \\(September 2025\\) for Sand Bodied Fl
 orida Boy. IG: @graysonwritespoems www.graysonwritespoems.com\n\nErnesto G
 aray\n\nErnesto M. Garay is the author of a poetry collection\, Reverberat
 ing Voices \\(Flowersong Press\, 2022\\). Garay was LA Revista Bilingüe: 
 La Voz’s Person of the Month in Sonoma County for March 2020\, and a Son
 oma County Discovered Award Recipient in Literary Arts. He is Ethnic Studi
 es faculty at Sierra College.\n\nAnika Snyder\n\nAnika Snyder was born and
  raised in Northern California. She published her first book\, Syllable So
 ccer\, in 2025 and is soon to release her second. She has been published i
 n Effable Press and performs her work regularly around Mendocino and Sonom
 a counties. IG: @anika366\n\nGary Weiner\n\nGary Weiner moved to Sonoma Co
 unty in 1973 and now resides in Sebastopol. A former working musician and 
 lawyer\, he released the full-length album Released at Last featuring Nin
 a Gerber and exhibits photography in galleries across San Francisco and Se
 bastopol. He is a prolific writer featured by the Sebastopol Center for th
 e Arts. IG: @gaweiner https://www.garyweinerarts.com/\n\nHosted by Josh Wi
 ndmiller \\+ Original Giotis!
LOCATION:The Big Easy
URL:https://foundpoets.org/events
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
