 nta Rosa Junior College are teaming up to transform the underutilized lawn
  throughout the school! This summer\, we sheet mulched 4 sections of lawn 
 and created a rain garden to help catch all our winter rain. This fall is 
 the right time to get native & climate-appropriate plantings in the ground
  before our winter season arrives!\n\nTogether\, we’ll create a water-wi
 se landscape that will build habitat and bring beauty to the school commun
 ity for years to come.\n\n**NOTE**: All are welcome (including children wi
 th adult supervision)\, and no experience is needed\n\nCome for some\, or 
 come for all—we will gather rain or shine!\n\n**We'll provide:**\n\n\\-F
 REE Lunch & Snacks\n\n\\-Instruction & tools\n\n\\-A fun day with the Peta
 luma and campus community\n\nWe look forward to seeing you there!\n\n**Hav
 e questions?** Reach out to us anytime by email to codyd@dailyacts.org or 
 by phone at (707) 696-4609
