BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Aspirations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T180000
UID:2609163c7oXYZ4M0aBlVYcFMWt7w
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  9/15/26\n\n**OCTOBER EXHIBIT: AS
 PIRATIONS**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES **– September 28 – October 25\, 2026**\n\
 n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, October 3\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Laura 
 Roney and Linda Loveland Reid and learn about their art and inspiration. 
  Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beau
 tiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma
  County artist\, **Laura Roney\,** unveils **Aspirations**\, a new collect
 ion of paintings in oil\, celebrating the unique differing goals people se
 t during our lives\, challenging us to take bold steps forward.  Of unive
 rsal inspiration**\, Aspiration and Awe** splashes the Milky Way’s starr
 y brilliance across the heavens\, capturing our imagination and hope as wo
 rldly cares are left behind.  Moving from natural forces to human endeavo
 r\, looking toward social change\, **Aspiring to Vote**\, the portrait of 
 a hopeful suffragette\, evokes the dream for a better future.  A lifetime
  goal for many\, the marathon\, **Aspiring for 26.2\,** captures the early
  morning excitement waiting for start times.  “People doing ordinary th
 ings but dreaming larger for the future has been a great inspiration for t
 his series.  I hope folks will be inspired by the boldness of people’s 
 dreams\,” commented Roney on her inspiration for the work.\n\nArt has be
 en a lifelong passion for Roney.  Beginning her art studies at a young ag
 e\, whatever avenue she was pursuing in life\, she continued her artistic 
 endeavors.  After a successful career in microbiology and pharmaceutical 
 research\, a family move to Northern California enabled Roney to focus on 
 her art.  She received her MFA from Academy of Art University\, San Franc
 isco.\n\nMeet the artist: Roney will host the Gallery on September 30 and 
 October 1 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features 
 Linda Loveland Reid’s **Intentional Chaos\,** a collection of exciting m
 ixed-media works that explode with excitement and energy. Random patterns\
 , amorphous shapes and dancing dribbles magically coalesce into bold state
 ments.  Intriguing and compelling\, like interlocking gears\, in **Patter
 ns of Memory** multiple patterns interlock on fields of gold and black.  
 “I love throwing ink\, paint and even coffee onto a blank canvas and cre
 ating through instinct\, gesture and emotion.  Distilling energy into sma
 ller works brings new challenges and some happy surprises\,” noted Reid 
 on her creative process.\n\nMeet the artist: Reid will host the Gallery on
  October 23 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\n Also join us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG
 **\, Thursday\, October 1\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1
 st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and crea
 tivity with over 20 galleries participating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nU
 pstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431
 -4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \
 n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvd
 rio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intro to California Coastal Range Geology
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T160000
UID:260910gZjGt-DpB0CnWYCYEUcMJQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us and explore Galbreath Preserve. Led by SSU’s Geology
  instructor Nicole Myers\, learn about geologic processes and climatic tre
 nds that comprise the natural forces of Northern California\, including wi
 ldfires\, floods and earthquakes. Find out how the California Coast Range 
 was formed by the same geologic events that shaped the Sierra Nevadas and 
 Central Valley of California. Learn how the coastal rocks that we live on 
 made it to California from the deep waters of the central Pacific Ocean\, 
 and how those rocks were changed by the forces of plate tectonics.
LOCATION:Galbreath Wildlands Preserve
URL:https://cei.sonoma.edu/coast-range-geology
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sweeney Todd
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
UID:260909mq2kZ9x1qUOi591H7s2k_A
DESCRIPTION:Sweeney Todd is largely considered one of Stephen Sondheim’s
  masterpieces. With it\, he aimed to create a musical that could “scare 
 the hell out of everyone\,” and yet\, somehow\, be funny.\n\nThe story c
 enters around Sweeney Todd\, an unjustly exiled barber who returns to Lond
 on\, seeking vengeance against the lecherous judge who framed him and rava
 ged his young wife. The road to revenge leads Todd to Mrs. Lovett\, a reso
 urceful proprietress of a failing pie shop\, above which\, he opens a new 
 barber practice. Mrs. Lovett’s luck sharply shifts when Todd’s thirst 
 for blood inspires the integration of an ingredient into her meat pies tha
 t has the people of 19th Century London lining up…and the carnage has on
 ly just begun!\n\n\\***Content Advisory:** Adult language and violent the
 mes\, as well as controversial pie recipes. Recommended for 12+.\n\nRunnin
 g Time: 2 hours\, 40 minutes including one intermission.\n\nOctober 23rd\,
  24th\, 25th\, \\*29th\, 30th\, 31st\, Nov 1st\, 6th\, 7th\, 8th.\n\nBook 
 by Hugh Wheeler\n\nMusic and Lyrics by Stephen Sondheim\n\nDirected by Ste
 ven David Martin\n\n**Friday and Saturday Shows:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Sunday Mat
 inee:** 2:00 PM\n\n**\\*Value Thursday:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Admission:** \n\nA
 dults: $44\n\nStudent w/ID: $10\n\n\\*Special Value Thursday Performanc
 e: Pay What You Can
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/sweeney-todd/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mike Annuzzi
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T130000
UID:260903-nZZXJrG002htHVFeRcvYA
DESCRIPTION:If you spent just a few minutes with Mike Annuzzi\, you would 
 become aware that his positivity towards life is contagious. Mike is alway
 s smiling. He is honest and expresses his feelings openly\, probably becau
 se he is a Capricorn.  Surrounded by the inspiration from his favorite tou
 r locations\, this California native maintains a blend of laid back coasta
 l attitude\, hustle of the big city life\, drive of Silicon Valley\, and r
 efinement and sophistication of wine country.  Mike started playing guitar
  and writing songs as a child. After the encouragement from friends throug
 hout his high school and college days\, he formed and fronted several band
 s. He discovered his passion in life on a stage performing original music.
   He is not the typical Polytechnic University graduate who landed a tech 
 job in Silicon Valley\, rather he sewed his roots and paved a path with a 
 musical career. Mike wrote and independently released The One \\(2016\\)\,
  Mike Annuzzi \\(2013\\)\, and Paradise \\(2012\\). In 2013\, Mike was cho
 sen West Coast Songwriters International Song Contest Singer/Songwriter of
  the Year for his single\, “Pay No Mind.” He also received Honorable M
 ention for “You Make Me Fall.” Mike's first single “Paradise” was 
 chosen as West Coast Songwriters San Francisco’s Song of the Year in 201
 0. His award-winning catalog has been featured on radio around California.
   With over 500 shows around the US in the last 3 years headlining clubs\,
  supporting national touring acts\, and developing residency performances 
 for venues around California\, Mike established himself and his positive r
 hythmic sound on hometown stages and beyond. He finds himself grateful to 
 have a career around his passion and knows it is attributed to the support
  of his family\, friends\, and fans.  Mike is always looking forward\, dev
 eloping his craft as a songwriter and performer\, and sharing his positive
  energy and passion at live shows.  Some stages Mike has been humbled to p
 erform:  BottleRock Napa Valley 2014 with headliners The Cure\, Outkast\, 
 and Eric Church \\(Over 80k tickets sold\\) The Mountain Winery\, Saratoga
  CA \\(Historic Santa Clara Valley 2k Seat Capacity Outdoor Venue\\) The C
 atalyst\, Santa Cruz CA \\(Iconic Music Venue host of acts from Neil Young
  to Nirvana\\)  Some of the artists Mike had the opportunity to play event
 s and share stages with include:  Los Lonely Boys \\(Single:  “Heaven”
  Top 20 Billboard Hit\\) Kenny Wayne Shepherd\, \\(“Blue On Black” rea
 ched \\#1 on Rock Charts\\). Colbie Caillat \\(Universal Republic Records\
 , Grammy Award Winning Artist\\) O.A.R. \\(Vangaurd Records\\) Edwin McCai
 n \\(Singer/Songwriter with Billboard hits including “I'll Be” and “
 I Could Not Ask For More”\\) Lukas Nelson \\(Promise of the Real\\) Jack
 ie Greene \\(Singer/Songwriter and Member of The Black Crowes\\) Tyrone We
 lls \\(Independent\, iTunes top 10 album artist\\)   Here is what others a
 re saying about Mike:  “He sings honestly and expressively and the writi
 ng shows sophistication.” -Paul Freeman\, Mercury News  “Mike Annuzzi 
 was a pleasure to watch...I loved the positivity of the songs and how full
  of joy Mike seemed to be filled with.” -Cadet Edac:  iheartsfbands.com 
  “Well\, listening to this wonderful artist it is clear that listeners a
 re in for a treat. His voice is divine and the smoothness of the whole thi
 ng just makes me feel alive and gearing to go! Perfect! -Skye McAdams:  Th
 e Daily Complains  “Check out this rising star.” -Glen Starkey:  New T
 imes SLO\, San Luis Obispo  Mike Annuzzi Plays Godin Guitars Silicon Valle
 y Based Singer/Songwriter\, Positive & Rhythmic Music and Lyrics. Check ou
 t Singer/Songwriter Mike Annuzzi.
LOCATION:Brassfield Estate Winery
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108558388?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
