BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dublinesque Album Release Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T210000
UID:260923ScEsapWdpUW0-BD72f4Kzw
DESCRIPTION:Don't miss this special evening where we'll take a musical tri
 p to Dublin with some of the Bay Area's finest musicians and singers! Eamo
 nn Flynn\, Darcy Noonan\, Hector Bragado and Felim Egan will dazzle us wit
 h their traditional and original "Dublinesque" harmonies. OCA favorites th
 rough and through\, we're just delighted to bring back this spirited\, tal
 ented group. Tickets are $25\, $20 for OCA members. Doors open at 6:30 PM.
  Refreshments available\, art gallery open during intermission.  Get Ticke
 ts  EAMONN FLYNN & DUBLINESQUE Eamonn Flynn forges his own brand of Irish 
 soul. The Dublin-born singer-songwriter/pianist got his start with The Com
 mitments\, a hit film about an Irish soul band\, and has since worked with
  American blues and R&B stars Elvin Bishop\, Maria Muldaur\, Evelyn Champa
 gne King\, Michael Franti & Spearhead\, Zigaboo Modeliste \\(The Meters\\)
 \, The Ray Charles Project\, and many more.  Flynn's new quartet DUBLINESQ
 UE brings his deep soul and gospel roots together with the Irish music tra
 ditions he was raised on.  "Dublinesque is my attempt to recreate the kind
  of parties we had in my parent's house\, growing up in Dublin\," explains
  Flynn. "There'd be neighbours and friends and it would always end up as a
  sing-song/jam session. Everyone would participate - if you couldn't hold 
 a tune you'd perform a 'recitation' or tell a joke!  "There was never any 
 delineation between genres of music - whether it was Irish tunes and balla
 ds\, soul music or a Beatles song\," he emphasizes.  The band brings toget
 her three talented Bay Area Irish traditional musicians: fellow Irishman F
 élim Egan \\(The Black Brothers\\) on accordion\, local favorite Darcy No
 onan on fiddle\, and from Basque country\, Spain\, Hector Bragado on banjo
 . They are also sometimes joined by special guests. Previous guests have i
 ncluded Glide Memorial Choir\, Maria Muldaur\, Mary Black\, Róisin O\, Mi
 chael Black\, Shay Black\, Autumn Rhodes\, Margaret Graham and dancers fro
 m the Kennelly\, Dillon and Whelan Schools of Irish Dance and the Cooley-K
 eegan Branch of Comhaltas Ceoltóiri.  "This is my chance to play with som
 e of my favorite musicians and recreate those parties!" says Flynn.  Flynn
 's latest of three solo albums is 'Anywhere But Home\,' celebrating Dublin
  from his San Francisco pandemic perspective. It received praise and wides
 pread airplay in the US\, Canada\, Europe and Australia.  "Flynn's songwri
 ting moves with true emotional register across history\, folklore and poet
 ry…with grit and true Dublin savvy." Deirdre Cronin - Irish Music Magazi
 ne
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/dublinesque
 -album-release-party
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:True West
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T203000
UID:260715FJptoGBaDkSc1K5kZP_-Zw
DESCRIPTION:Set in a suburban California home\, True West follows two brot
 hers with sharply contrasting personalities who reunite while house-sittin
 g for their mother. One is a disciplined\, aspiring screenwriter\, while t
 he other lives a more nomadic and unpredictable life. As they reconnect\, 
 their interactions shift from uneasy familiarity to intense competition\, 
 fueled by conflicting ambitions and long-standing tensions. Shepard's play
  delves into themes of authenticity\, creativity\, and the myth of the Ame
 rican frontier\, using sharp dialogue and dark humor to reveal the instabi
 lity beneath the surface of everyday life. As the brothers' dynamic evolve
 s\, the boundaries between their identities begin to blur\, raising questi
 ons about who they are and what defines them.
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/true-west/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
