X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Timely Wisdom
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T190000
UID:261029vFLAfkX5n0ir7P1X9baaJQ
DESCRIPTION:The Power of Storytelling in Troubling Times\n\nWe will explor
 e storytelling as a creative way to wield the liberating power of the Dhar
 ma in our daily lives\, especially in these troubling times.  \n\nDrawin
 g on the lifelong commitments of Paula Arai’s research-based writing as 
 a contemplative practice and Kathie Fischer’s focus on Zen practice in d
 omestic and monastic modes\, we will invite people to help us create our o
 wn community story about wielding the compassionate teaching of the Dharma
  in these times.
LOCATION:The Glaser Center
URL:https://events.humanitix.com/https-events-humanitix-com-timely-wisdom-
 2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Park Admission for Veterans and Active Military
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T170000
UID:261028FTkUJrE3eUm-ZbvLJwffQg
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of their service to the United States\, Jack Lo
 ndon State Historic Park will provide free admission to all active-duty mi
 litary and veterans on Nov. 7\, 8\, 9\, 10\, and 11 - Veterans Day – 202
 6.\n\nBlending the fascinating history of one of America’s most prolific
  and successful writers with the serenity of nature\, Jack London State Hi
 storic Park offers more than 29 miles of back-country trails that roam thr
 ough mixed forests\, redwood groves\, oak woodlands\, and grassy meadows i
 n Sonoma County’s Valley of the Moon.  \n\nActive duty or retired mili
 tary identification or form DD214 can be presented at the entry kiosk to r
 eceive free admission.\n\nAdmission\, regularly priced at $15\, covers one
  vehicle of up to nine passengers for the day.  Park hours are 9 a.m. to 
 5 p.m. daily.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park - Oak Grove Picnic Area (standing
  capacity)
URL:http://www.jacklondonpark.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mary Collins School at Cherry Valley Presents Beetlejuice JR
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T140000
UID:261026crfv9GOOwUqUjSXp9imnXQ
DESCRIPTION:Something strange and unusual is coming to Mary Collins at Che
 rry Valley School! The school's Theater Arts Program \\(TAP\\) presents Be
 etlejuice JR.\, running October 30–November 8\, 2026\, featuring two cas
 ts of talented young performers and a student technical crew bringing the 
 beloved Broadway musical to life.\n\nUnder the leadership of Darby Ciampi\
 , Lindsey Nettleton\, and an experienced creative team\, TAP delivers an a
 mbitious theatrical experience that goes far beyond the stage. Students ar
 e involved in every aspect of production\, from acting\, singing\, and cho
 reography to lighting\, sound\, set construction\, costumes\, and props. W
 ith professional mentorship\, students gain hands-on experience in the ful
 l theatrical process\, developing creativity\, confidence\, and collaborat
 ion along the way.
LOCATION:Mary Collins School at Cherry Vallet
URL:https://my.cheddarup.com/c/mccv-beetlejuice-jr/items
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
