BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Uncovering Sonoma Terroir: What's Really in Your Vineyard Soil? 
 🍇
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T200000
UID:2610282Z2biOLtkk2pZf7x9nvgZQ
DESCRIPTION:Have you wondered why Pinot lovers talk about Goldridge soil? 
 Or maybe you’ve been trying to figure out why some areas of your vineyar
 d just don’t seem to produce as well as others. The answer might be righ
 t under your feet! Come to our November 12 meeting to learn more about the
  soils of Sonoma and the criticality of matching rootstock\, variety and s
 oil to get the best out of your vineyard.\n\nDr. Paul Anamosa will discuss
  these intricacies on November 12th at the Sonoma Community Center during 
 a presentation hosted by Sonoma Home Winemakers. Titled *"It’s Soil\, n
 ot Dirt! – The Importance of Soil Analysis in Making Better Wine\,"* th
 e session details the soils of Sonoma County and highlights how understand
 ing soil composition\, structure\, and chemistry helps winemakers and enth
 usiasts make smarter decisions from vine to glass.\n\n📍 Sonoma Communi
 ty Center\, Room 110\, 276 E. Napa St. Sonoma\n\n⏰ Doors open at 6:30 p
 .m. | Presentation at 7:00 p.m.\n\n🍷 Free and open to the public (21+ 
 for wine tasting\; please bring your own glass and winemakers\, a bottle t
 o share for the evening).
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:http://Sonomahomewine.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
