UID:261030e6jYg_kIWUigBkcwbHJqdQ
DESCRIPTION:Whether you’re catching up on winning films you missed durin
 g the festival weekend or experiencing our lineup for the very first time\
 , join us for the ultimate “Best of the Fest–Audience Favorites” sho
 wcase! Selected directly by audience votes across all 8 screening blocks f
 rom our 5th annual festival\, this curated one-day retrospective brings to
 gether 12 to-rated short films from 7 countries.\n\nThis special program i
 ncludes two winning films unanimously selected by both the audience and ou
 r jury\, featuring cultural icon musician/actor Tom Waits\, screenwriter B
 illy Ray (*The Hunger Games*)\, Ed Begley Jr.\, and other distinguished ar
 tists. Visit our site for full jury bios and film details.\n\n**Schedule &
  Screening Blocks:**\n\nThe films are split across two 90-minute programs 
 (Block A and Block B). Intermissions offer plenty of time to enjoy a coffe
 e\, bite\, or wine tasting in downtown Healdsburg:\n\n**Option 1:** Block
  A at 1:30 PM – Block B at 4:30 PM\n\n**Option 2:** Block B at 4:30 PM 
 – Block A (Encore) at 7:30 PM\n\n**1:30 PM** – Block A\n\n**4:30 PM**
  – Block B\n\n**7:30 PM** – Block A (Evening Encore)\n\n**Tickets & 
 Pricing:**\n\n**Single Block:** $20\n\n**Day Pass (All Blocks):** $30
LOCATION: Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://healdsburgfilm.com/2026-audience-favorites-screening-nov-14-20
 26/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pine Needle Basketmaking with Judith Thomas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T150000
UID:261029hzLbsxb7c0iPpcC92xcvRw
DESCRIPTION:Slow down and spend a few hours learning the contemplative art
  of pine needle basket making with Judith Thomas. Using Oaxacan pine needl
 es gathered right here at Western Hills Garden\, participants will learn t
 he techniques for coiling and stitching a basket by hand. The process requ
 ires patience and focus\, but that’s part of its pleasure. Judith will o
 ffer expert guidance throughout\, making this a welcoming workshop for beg
 inners as well as those with experience. Come make something beautiful fro
 m the Garden\, one stitch at a time.\n\nAll materials included. Snacks\, h
 ot and cold drinks\, and a simple vegan lunch provided.  Please bring you
 r own if you have dietary restrictions\n\nInstructor bio: Judith Thomas wa
 s one of the founding parents of the East Bay Waldorf School and a member 
 of the faculty as a class teacher (1985-1993) and handwork teacher (1994-2
 007) in both the lower school and in the high school. She has been a weave
 r and fiber artist for many years and currently teaches pine needle basket
 ry classes and weaving workshops across the Bay Area.
LOCATION:Western Hills Garden
URL:https://www.westernhillsgarden.com/programs/pineneedlebasket2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
