BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pop-up Workshop: Paper Clay Abstraction with Gabriel John Poucher
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T160000
UID:261024nG3OxFDeCE6LGQryobC_PA
DESCRIPTION:This workshop will explore the unique possibilities of paper c
 lay\, with a focus on process-drive sculpture. We will cover nontraditiona
 l building techniques\, using slip as a decorative material\, and creating
  structure through the use of components. The workshop will feature a lect
 ure explaining the unique materials we’ll be using\, followed by a multi
 -part demo and activities. Participants will be provided with materials an
 d are encouraged to investigate playfully\, with a focus on process over o
 utcomes.This workshop coincides with Gabriel’s Solo Exhibition\, Burgeon
 \, on view at the Sonoma Community Center from November 7 – 29. Gabriel
 ’s work stems from the intersection of ecology and queer identity\, and 
 the parallel frameworks they provide for resisting rigid categories\, bina
 ry distinctions\, and expected outcomes. Burgeon examines the notion that 
 transformation does not require resolution. The work draws inspiration fro
 m natural processes of growth and consumption\, and the way they blur the 
 boundaries between organism and environment\, individual and collective. C
 onstructing clay forms through an extended process of repetition and accum
 ulation\, pattern and deviation\, Gabriel’s work explores the idea that 
 to be in flux is not to be incomplete.Saturday\, November 14\, 2026 12:00 
 pm to 4:00 pm\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\nCategory\n\nCer
 amics\, Workshops\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRe
 gistration Cost:\n\n$65\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$10\n\nTotal Registration Cos
 t:\n\n$75
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/paper-clay-abstraction/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Our Wild Watershed- Owl Hill Film Screening & Q&A
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T184500
UID:261023Eg4jLvnjD0KVRuPQ8Is8EQ
DESCRIPTION:Join the Laguna de Santa Rosa Foundation for a special evening
  in our Our Wild Watershed series featuring a screening of Owl Hill\, a 15
 -minute documentary exploring the community of owl box keepers and preserv
 ationists working to support and protect owls in the San Francisco Bay Are
 a\, particularly in Sonoma and Marin counties. The film features Laguna Fo
 undation volunteer Nick Jones\, who helped establish and monitor our Barn 
 Owl box cameras at the Laguna Environmental Center. Following the screenin
 g\, filmmaker Sean Restivo will join Nick and representatives from All Abo
 ut Owls\, a local organization dedicated to owl conservation and environme
 ntal education\, for a conversation and Q&A about the film\, local owl con
 servation\, and the community working to protect these remarkable birds.
LOCATION:Laguna Environmental Center
URL:https://OWWOwls26.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fitness Is Better Together: Community Meetup hosted by Kae Method
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T120000
UID:261022uFRocifHwEWFFXy6Q9Gi-A
DESCRIPTION:Fitness is better when we do it together!\n\nJoin us for the f
 irst Kae Method Community Meetup\, a free outdoor fitness experience desig
 ned to bring people together through movement\, encouragement\, and meanin
 gful connections.\n\nWhether you're just beginning your fitness journey\, 
 getting back into a routine\, or already enjoy working out\, this event is
  for you. Coach Kae will lead an accessible\, full-body workout featuring 
 strength\, mobility\, and functional movements\, with options for differen
 t fitness levels and abilities. You can participate at your own pace while
  enjoying the energy and encouragement of exercising alongside others.\n\n
 This is also an opportunity to meet new people\, build friendships\, and b
 ecome part of a growing fitness community right here in Santa Rosa.\n\nCom
 e on your own\, bring a friend\, or invite someone who could use a little 
 extra motivation. We'll create opportunities to connect throughout the exp
 erience\, with time afterward to relax\, socialize\, and get to know one a
 nother.\n\nWhat to Expect\n\nAn accessible\, coach-led workout: A full-bo
 dy fitness experience with modifications and challenges for different abil
 ity levels.\n\nSupportive coaching: Guidance and encouragement from Kae t
 o help you move with confidence.\n\nCommunity connections: Opportunities 
 to meet people\, encourage one another\, and build relationships.\n\nA wel
 coming environment: No matter your fitness experience\, you'll have a pla
 ce here.\n\nWhat to Bring\n\nWear comfortable workout clothes and supporti
 ve athletic shoes. Bring water\, a towel\, and an exercise mat if you have
  one.\n\nEvent Details\n\nDate: Saturday\, November 14\, 2026\n\nTime: 1
 0:00 AM\n\nLocation: Finley Community Park\, Santa Rosa\, California\n\nC
 ost: Free\n\nWho Can Attend: Adults 18\\+ of all fitness experience leve
 ls\n\nRegistration is required because space is limited.\n\nAll participan
 ts will be asked to sign a liability waiver before joining the workout. Pl
 ease arrive a few minutes early to complete check-in.\n\nReserve your spot
  and join us as we kick off the Kae Method Community!\n\nLet's move togeth
 er\, grow stronger\, and stay connected.
LOCATION:Finley Community Park
URL:https://www.kaemethod.com/event-details/fitness-is-better-together-com
 munity-meetup-hosted-by-kae-method
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
