SUMMARY:BellyDancing with Carem
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261116T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261116T190000
UID:2610129KLRMelTq0SQ63mwfuOYSQ
DESCRIPTION:Bellydancing for Beginners \n\nDiscover the beauty of Raqs Sh
 arqi \\(bellydance\\). This beginner-friendly class introduces you to fou
 ndational bellydance technique\, including hip movements\, isolations\, un
 dulations\, traveling steps\, combinations and musicality. You’ll develo
 p coordination\, body awareness\, strength\, and confidence while learning
  to move with greater ease and expression.\n\nNo previous dance experience
  is required. All bodies and experience levels are welcome.\n\nCome move t
 o the music\, connect with your body\, and discover the joy of bellydancin
 g\n\nCAREM LOVE\n\nCarem Love is a wellness advocate\, professional dancer
 \, and certified yoga instructor with a Bachelor’s degree in Dance. She 
 has extensive training in Bellydance\, a deep passion for Latin dance\, an
 d is certified in Hatha\, Vinyasa\, and Children’s Yoga.\n\nBelly dance 
 has profoundly supported her health\, well-being\, and dance career\, insp
 iring her to help others experience the same body-mind benefits. In her cl
 asses\, students learn to connect more deeply with themselves.\n\nDATE: Mo
 nday\n\nTIME: 6:00 PM\n\nWHERE: Salsa Dance Marin\, 4140 Redwood Hwy 8\, S
 an Rafael
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/belly-dancing-with-carem/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maple Magic & Winter Wonder
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261116T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261116T170000
UID:260824FAc5WjjQG0Oi1SSzTnz2zw
DESCRIPTION:As the days grow shorter and cooler\, Sonoma Botanical Garden 
 transforms with the beauty of the changing seasons. From the first signs o
 f autumn in October to the brilliant display of rare Asian maples in Nov
 ember and the quiet beauty of early winter in December\, each visit offer
 s something new to discover. \n\n*Maple Magic* *& Winter Wonder* invites
  visitors to experience this special time of year through nature\, creativ
 ity\, and connection. Throughout the season\, the Garden offers guided wal
 ks\, hands-on workshops\, lectures\, and special experiences inspired by t
 he changing landscape. Wander among vibrant fall foliage\, breathe in the 
 sweet fragrance of katsura trees\, enjoy creative programs\, and experienc
 e the peaceful beauty of the Garden as it transitions into winter.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Salsa Beginners 2 - Mondays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261116T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261116T190000
UID:260427kpwe_k6cskK9nLQuNvb4mg
DESCRIPTION:Ready to take your salsa to the next level? Salsa lessons in M
 arin will help you to add some flair and fluidity to your salsa dancing.\n
 \nPre-requisite: Salsa Beginners 1 – You know your basic steps\, left tu
 rn\, right turn\, cross-body lead\, and you hold your frame.\n\nWhat You
 ’ll Learn\n\nWe’ve curated a curriculum designed to build your confide
 nce and your “social dance” vocabulary:\n\n• The Cross Body Lead (CB
 L) Series: Master both Inside and Outside Turns\, the essential building b
 locks for moving your partner across the floor with grace.\n\n• The “I
  Turn – You Turn”: A classic social dance staple that develops timing 
 and hand-change coordination.\n\n• The Walk-Through: Learn how to transi
 tion smoothly through the dance space without breaking your rhythm.\n\n•
  Footwork & Shine: We’ll break down the footwork pattern that adds perso
 nality to your “shines.”\n\nTechnique & Artistry\n\n• Dancing is abo
 ut more than just where your feet go. In this level\, we dive deeper into 
 the “how”:\n\n• The Frame: Understand the “tension and compression
 ” needed to lead and follow clearly without using muscle.\n\n• Upper B
 ody Mechanics: Learn how to isolate your ribcage and shoulders to move wit
 h that authentic Latin soul.\n\n• Connection: Developing a “heavy” b
 ut responsive arm connection to ensure your partner feels every lead.\n\nI
 mportant Details\n\n• No dance experience required: Whether you’ve nev
 er danced before or it’s been a while\, you’re welcome here!\n\n• No
  partner necessary: Come solo or bring a friend—either way\, you’ll ha
 ve plenty of opportunities to dance.\n\n• Please wear non-marking shoe s
 oles: This helps us keep our dance floor in great condition.\n\nDate & Tim
 e:\n\nMonday 6:00 PM\n\nSaturday 11:00 AM\n\nInstructor: Lucie Ebnerova\n\
 nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway #8 San Rafael\, CA (salsa lessons in Marin)
 \n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allowed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/salsa-beginners-2/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
