DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T193000
UID:260317PP7mJQlesUOPJ2__Yvwz9Q
DESCRIPTION:Your First Steps into Bachata\n\nThis class is perfect for bac
 hata beginners that want to learn basic steps and skills\, or those who wa
 nt to refresh their foundational skills. We understand that learning somet
 hing new can feel a little intimidating. That’s why our supportive and r
 elaxed environment is specifically designed to make learning bachata basic
 s an absolute blast!\n\nOur friendly instructors will guide you through:\n
 \n**Basic directional steps:** You’ll learn the fundamental movements t
 hat form the building blocks of all bachata dancing.\n\n**Proper frame for
  partner work:** Discover how to connect comfortably and effectively with
  a partner\, setting you up for smooth and enjoyable dances.\n\n**Simple t
 urn patterns:** We’ll introduce you to easy-to-follow turn patterns tha
 t will have you dancing with a partner in no time.\n\nWe’ve carefully or
 ganized our curriculum to ensure that each movement is easy to grasp and r
 emember\, building your confidence with every step. Our goal is to make le
 arning fun. Join us to learn Bachata in Marin.\n\nImportant Details\n\n**N
 o dance experience required:** Whether you’ve never danced before or it
 ’s been a while\, you’re welcome here!\n\n**No partner necessary:** C
 ome solo or bring a friend—either way\, you’ll have plenty of opportun
 ities to dance.\n\nPlease wear **non-marking shoe soles:** This helps us
  keep our dance floor in great condition.\n\nCome join us and discover the
  joy of bachata! We can’t wait to see you on the dance floor.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/bachata-beginners/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Napa Bookmine Book Club: The Wedding People by Alison Espach
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T180000
UID:2610210-wBhWSr8Eqfd82Y25S7zg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a book club discussion! This year\, 2026\, Napa Bo
 okmine Book Clubs' book picks will come straight from home\, this year's N
 apa Bookmine BINGO Card! Each book will match a BINGO square. Hurrah! Play
  along with Napa Bookmine and read some new\, fun books\, and if you come 
 to every meeting\, you may get a BINGO in the meantime. \;\\) This is a fr
 ee event\, but we would appreciate your RSVP so we can plan for your atten
 dance! Questions? Email us at events@napabookmine.com ABOUT THE BOOK The r
 unaway New York Times bestselling Today Show Read With Jenna Book Club Pic
 k\, with more than 1.5 million copies sold\, about an unexpected wedding g
 uest and the surprising people who help her start anew. Named a Best Book 
 of the Year by The Guardian\, Time\, Chicago Tribune\, Elle\, Real Simple\
 , and Glamour. It’s a beautiful day in Newport\, Rhode Island\, when Pho
 ebe Stone arrives at the grand Cornwall Inn wearing a green dress and gold
  heels\, not a bag in sight\, alone. She’s immediately mistaken by every
 one in the lobby for one of the wedding people\, but she’s actually the 
 only guest at the Cornwall who isn’t here for the big event. Phoebe is h
 ere because she’s dreamed of coming for years—she hoped to shuck oyste
 rs and take sunset sails with her husband\, only now she’s here without 
 him\, at rock bottom\, and determined to have one last decadent splurge on
  herself. Meanwhile\, the bride has accounted for every detail and every p
 ossible disaster the weekend might yield except for\, well\, Phoebe and Ph
 oebe's plan—which makes it that much more surprising when the two women 
 can’t stop confiding in each other. In turns absurdly funny and devastat
 ingly tender\, Alison Espach’s The Wedding People is ultimately an incre
 dibly nuanced and resonant look at the winding paths we can take to places
  we never imagined—and the chance encounters it sometimes takes to rerou
 te us. ABOUT THE AUTHOR Alison Espach is the bestselling author of The Wed
 ding People\, a New York Times Editor’s Choice\, a Today Show Read With 
 Jenna Book Club Pick\, a Barnes and Noble Book Club Pick\, and a \\#1 Indi
 e Next Pick. The Wedding People spent several dozen weeks on the New York 
 Times Best Seller list and will be published in over 35 countries. She is 
 also the author of Notes on Your Sudden Disappearance\, a Chicago Tribune 
 and NPR “Best Book of the Year\,” as well as The Adults\, a New York T
 imes Editor’s Choice and Barnes and Noble Discover Pick. Her fictional a
 udio series In-Depth Market Research Interviews with Dead People is an Aud
 ible Original. She has written for McSweeney’s\, Vogue\, Outside\, LitHu
 b\, Joyland and other places. She lives and teaches creative writing in Rh
 ode Island. Alison received her MFA from Washington University in St. Loui
 s. She has been a writer-in-residence at the Ucross Foundation for the Art
 s\, Millay Arts\, The Wassaic Project\, the Cuttyhunk Writers Residency an
 d the San Miguel Literary Sala.
LOCATION:Napa Bookmine
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1768682874182370/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
