BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Olio Nuovo Harvest and Milling Experience at Gold Ridge Organic Fa
 rms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T141500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T153000
UID:261021eWlej4XmqEeMzZ3u86mjAw
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an unforgettable behind-the-scenes journey into th
 e heart of our olive harvest season. This experience offers a rare opportu
 nity to see how our award-winning olive oil is crafted\, from the branches
  of our olive trees to the first drops of the season’s oil.\n\nYour jour
 ney begins with a guided tour of our 88-acre organic farm. You’ll step i
 nto the orchards to watch our expert team harvest fresh olives straight fr
 om the trees at their peak of flavor.\n\nNext\, you’ll visit our state-o
 f-the-art olive oil mill\, where you’ll learn about the milling process 
 and see the olives pressed into vibrant\, fresh Olio Nuovo\, the celebrate
 d “new oil” prized by culinary enthusiasts for its brilliant green hue
  and robust\, peppery finish.\n\nThe highlight comes right at the source: 
 tasting fresh Olio Nuovo straight from the mill just moments after the oli
 ves are crushed.\n\nBook now to secure your spot for this rare\, behind-th
 e-scenes look at our harvest traditions.\n\nImportant Notes: Please wear c
 omfortable shoes suitable for walking on a working farm This outdoor exper
 ience may be canceled due to wet weather. Full refund available.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/627571/olio
 -nuovo-harvest-and-milling-experience
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:STIMULANT: Art as Remedy for Diseased Culture\, Exhibition and Eve
 nts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T160000
UID:261021bEui6f9T5kGAzNrZlMez2Q
DESCRIPTION:In a diseased society with failing systems\, what can we do to
  turn things around? For two weeks a new exhibition from Sonoma County’s
  own Apocalypse Studio\, a father and daughter artist duo\, STIMULANT: Ar
 t as Remedy for Diseased Culture proposes that art is the antidote and cr
 eativity is the countermove. This exhibition explores the inner and outer 
 work of co-creating that antidote: art that stimulates society’s creativ
 ity - the social sculpture we all create together. There will be two perfo
 rmances\, two lectures\, a Parisian -style Art Salon\, and times to visit 
 the large exhibition and talk with the artists. All events are free to at
 tend. Visit www.apocalypse.art/stimulant for details and schedule of event
 s.
LOCATION:Laguna Lab
URL:https://apocalypse.art/stimulant/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
