BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wreckless Strangers at Rancho Nicasio
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
UID:260905SeG_dLzSc0-UcOSuF2mRSw
DESCRIPTION:Fresh off a busy summer of performances across the Bay Area an
 d tour stops in Littleton\, Colorado\, and Jackson Hole\, Wyoming\, Wreckl
 ess Strangers return this fall with a trio of Northern California shows\, 
 highlighted by an appearance at Hardly Strictly Bluegrass in San Francisco
 's Golden Gate Park. The band will also perform at the historic Paper Mill
  Creek Saloon in Forest Knolls on September 18 and Rancho Nicasio on Frida
 y\, November 20\, while continuing to build momentum with national radio a
 irplay and a climb up the Top 50 Americana and AAA Singles charts.\n\nWith
  Dirty Souls\, Wreckless Strangers return to their rock-and-roll roots\, d
 elivering their rawest and most visceral studio effort to date. The six-so
 ng collection channels the arena rock spirit of the '70s and '80s that sha
 ped the band's earliest influences while bringing a fresh\, modern edge to
  the sound. The first single\, "Dirty Soul\," continues to receive nationa
 l airplay and is available on major streaming platforms. The full album wa
 s released in March.\n\nWreckless Strangers is a collective of friends and
  musicians carrying the torch for San Francisco’s grand rock ‘n’ rol
 l tradition. Their unique blend of “Ameri-Cali Soul” melds the contemp
 orary blues stylings of Bonnie Raitt and Boz Scaggs\; the songwriting sens
 ibilities of Sons of Champlin and Fleetwood Mac\; the swashbuckling Americ
 ana of the Lost Planet Airmen and Peter Rowan\; and the funk of Sly Stone 
 and Tower of Power with a dash of Grateful Dead and Jefferson Airplane for
  flavor and unpredictability. With soaring vocal harmonies and burning ins
 trumental improvisation\, framed by concise\, poignant original songwritin
 g\, Wreckless Strangers seek to honor and carry forth the brand of free-sp
 irited musical fun and adventure that defines the Bay Area. \n\nThe band 
 features Amber Morris on lead vocals\; David Noble on lead guitar and lead
  vocals\; Joshua Zucker on bass and vocals\; Mick Hellman on drums and voc
 als\; Rob Anderson on guitar and vocals\; and Fletcher Nielsen on keys. \
 n\nDirty Souls is the band’s third studio outing under the tutelage of G
 rammy-winning producer Dave Way\, who fosters a level of depth and organic
  cohesion that firmly establishes Wreckless Strangers in San Francisco’s
  storied rock ’n’ roll legacy. The songwriting is among their most int
 imate and personal\, exploring themes of relationships\, loss\, empowermen
 t\, and perseverance. Co-lead singers Amber Morris and David Noble functio
 n as a single organism\, bringing the songs to life with bluesy grit\, sou
 l\, and humanity bolstered by rock-solid\, road-hewn grooves.
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio
URL:http://ranchonicasio.com/events/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
