BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Comedian Don Friesen
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T203000
UID:261003hLXxBqOT7U-tpxuzyUxbcw
DESCRIPTION:The Laugh Cellar presents: \n\nLos Angeles-based Don Friesen 
 is an award-winning headliner comedian known for his high-energy\, physica
 l\, and sharply relatable comedy. The only two-time winner in the 50-year 
 history of the San Francisco Comedy Competition\, Friesen has appeared on 
 Showtime\, Netflix\, Amazon Prime\, Comedy Central\, Dry Bar Comedy\, and 
 SiriusXM. Friesen blends observational comedy\, storytelling\, improvisati
 on\, and physicality into a style all his own. His latest special\, *Break
  a Leg*\, finds Friesen older\, possibly wiser\, and—spoiler alert—not
  quite as married as he used to be. Whether navigating technology\, relati
 onships\, or the absurdities of everyday life\, Friesen has a knack for tu
 rning real-life chaos into big laughs.\n\nIndoor Event - Balletto Vineyard
 s Reserve Room\n\nTheater style seating\n\nWine by the bottle and savory s
 nacks available for purchase. \n\n21+ \n\nDoors 6:00 PM
LOCATION:Balletto Vineyards
URL:https://www.crushersofcomedy.com/november212026.html
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:International Film:  PRIMAVERA
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T180000
UID:260929VDz-rZ3B3kGdgGvooX7OHg
DESCRIPTION:Music and power intertwine in Primavera\, as Antonio Vivaldi t
 eaches an orphan how to imagine a new destiny for herself.\n\nA talented v
 iolinist\, Cecilia\, confined in an orphanage\, meets Vivaldi who becomes 
 her teacher. Under his mentorship and through his music\, she gains courag
 e to break free from the life she was destined for and pursue her passion.
 \n\nVenice\, early 18th century. Renowned for its exceptional music progra
 m\, the Pièta orphanage is home to Cecilia\, a 20-year-old violin virtuos
 o. Despite her extraordinary talent\, Cecilia remains confined within the 
 orphanage and like all the girls there\, her only escape seems to get marr
 ied. Yet\, her life changes drastically when Antonio Vivaldi\, a brilliant
  and ambitious composer\, arrives as the new violin teacher. Through a com
 plex artistic relationship with Vivaldi and his music\, Cecilia finds the 
 strength to challenge the destiny that once seemed inevitable.
LOCATION:Jarvis Conservatory
URL:https://jarvisconservatory.ticketspice.com/primavera
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
