BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack London Gravesite Memorial
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T120000
UID:261028qdgER9swP0OB5GwQBAXs1Q
DESCRIPTION:Jack London died of kidney failure on Nov. 22\, 1916. In his s
 hort life he accomplished much\, not only as a writer of fifty books\, but
  also as an adventurer\, reporter\, war correspondent\, sports article wri
 ter\, and innovative farmer. He was in the process of developing a model r
 anch\, destined to be the finest in California\, when he died. He would ha
 ve wished farming to be his true legacy\, far beyond writing. Learn more a
 bout the gravesite.\n\nOn the 110th anniversary of his passing - Nov. 22\,
  2026 - Volunteer Park Historian Lou Leal will preside over a service at L
 ondon’s gravesite.  Songwriter and vocalist Jeff Falconer will perform 
 his original song\, written in memory of Jack London.\n\nThe memorial is o
 pen to the public at no charge. The park entry fee of $15 per vehicle appl
 ies.  Those attending should gather at the House of Happy Walls Museum at
  10:30 a.m. to start the half mile walk to the grave site.  A golf cart w
 ill be available for those who need assistance.\n\nIn the event of rain\, 
 the memorial will be held on the second floor in the museum which can only
  be reached by stairway.  For information about accessibility\, call 707-
 938-5216.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park - Event venues (overall park limi
 t)
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/gravesite-memorial-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Flight Lessons: A Folk Opera by Deborah Crooks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T164500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T190000
UID:261026gNUk1w2exkiggJ-ZdEePWw
DESCRIPTION:Based on a true story about Peregrine Falcons and humans livin
 g at the intersection of wild and urban habitats\, "Flight Lessons" is a t
 wo-act\, multi-character folk opera exploring themes of home\, adaptation 
 and recovery. The narrative-in-song follows an urban wildlife biologist wh
 o monitors the breeding pair of Peregrine Falcons nesting on a bridge and 
 how their lives intersect with the human inhabitants of the neighborhood a
 fter one of the birds is shot.  "Flight Lessons"  draws upon Deborah's e
 xperiences studying natural history and raptor conservation and features a
 n ensemble cast including Deborah\, Kwame Copeland\, Sean Lightholder\, Ka
 ren Mitchell\, Liz Stuart and Mick Shaffer.\n\n“FLIGHT LESSONS is a full
 \, rich story—the heroine’s journey—that takes us into the world of 
 urban birds.…remarkable and moving.”— Alameda Post\n\nhttps://debora
 hcrooks.com/flight-lessons
LOCATION:The Lost Church Santa Rosa
URL:https://tinyurl.com/FlightLessonsNov22
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Disney's Frozen the Broadway Musical
