BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma's 10th Annual Holiday Food Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T200000
UID:261028RXdCC8xqF0GvDyHA9wh64A
DESCRIPTION:Mon Nov 23rd 3:00-8:00 An Indoor Farmer's Market - Purchase Di
 rectly From Local Artisans & Prepare for the Holidays!\n\nholidayfoodfair.
 com for a list of vendors\n\n**Mon Nov 23rd 3:00 to 8:00**: (The Monday be
 fore Thanksgiving) The Petaluma Holiday Food Fair is an indoor farmer’s 
 market where folks can purchase directly from local food artisans to prepa
 re for thanksgiving and beyond. This year\, for the first time\, we are ho
 sting our annual event at our distillery (Barber Lee Spirits) in downtown 
 Petaluma\, where fair attendees will also have the opportunity to taste ou
 r spirits and enjoy seasonal cocktails and libations while they shop and e
 njoy our extensive holiday decorations!\n\n**FREE tickets and reservations
  are required\, and will book your timeslot for entry.**\n\n**Kids do not
  require tickets.**\n\nAfter the 2017 wildfires devastated Sonoma County\,
  Lorraine & Michael Barber of the Brutal Hill Winery noticed that many of 
 the local artisans they supported in their tasting room were suffering fro
 m lack of business. At the height of harvest season\, farmers markets were
  closed and sales were slim. They organized this event to get a much neede
 d financial boost to local food producers. The event has become a vital st
 art to the holiday season and remains an important and beloved event for l
 ocal food artisans and Sonoma County residents to kick off the holiday sea
 son!\n\nSampling is up to the discretion of the individual vendors. Beer\,
  Wine\, Cocktails\, and Non-Alcoholic drinks will be available for consump
 tion onsite. The number of people allowed in at one time is limited. Ticke
 ts are free and include a time preference (15 minute increments) so there
 ’s less of a wait and some more space. **Kids do not require tickets!**
LOCATION:Barber Lee Spirits
URL:http://holidayfoodfair.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
