BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:November Soda Club Firing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261125T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261125T190000
UID:261030TLbV-n7HjEKK3cu6B0v3Og
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, Sunday\, and Wednesday\n\nDates & Times\n\nSaturday
 \, November 21\, 2026 10:00 AM – 5:00 PM\n\nSunday\, November 22\, 2026 
 10:00 AM – 6:00 PM \\*Time is subject to change\n\nWednesday\, November 
 25\, 2026\n\n\\*unload date subject to change based on club consensus 4:00
  Pm – 7:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nKiln Shed\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Worksho
 ps\n\nExperience Level\n\nIntermediate and Advanced\n\nAges\n\n17+\n\nRegi
 stration Cost:\n\n$110\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$15\n\nTotal Registration Cost
 :\n\n$125 **Prerequisites to enroll in Soda Firing Club**:\n\nMust have ta
 ken at least one\, Intro to Mid-Range Soda Firing Workshop\n\nBe well vers
 ed in protocols for loading the soda kiln\, kiln safety\, equipment and op
 erating safety\, and be willing and able to be unsupervised with the kiln 
 during loading\, unloading\, and post firing cleaning of the kiln.\n\nMust
  have pre-approval from the Director of Ceramics or Soda Club Facilitator\
 n\n**program overview**\n\nThe “Julia” Soda Firing Club is designed fo
 r folks looking for longterm use with our Soda Kiln\, Julia. The club is l
 ed by Studio Monitors\, and a Studio Technician but involves no formal ins
 truction in soda firing processes. Without a formalized instructor\, our S
 oda Club offers a more financially accessible way of having work soda-fire
 d\, without the need to retake our Intro to Soda Firing workshop courses. 
 The Soda Club will run firings monthly or as often as desired and needed d
 epending on participant interest. Unlike our Soda Firing Workshops\, club 
 firings will include no instruction on wadding\, slips\, glazes\, or any l
 ectures on the subject of soda firing. As such\, participants must feel co
 mfortable with the safety and care of the equipment\, as well as loading\,
  firing\, and maintenance procedures surrounding the firing process. **Eac
 h participant gets 1 cubic foot of firing space. (Tip\; Make sure all your
  pots fit approximately into a milk crate which is 1 cubic foot of space).
 (Tip\; Make sure all your pots fit approximately into a milk crate which i
 s 1 cubic foot of space).**
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/november-soda-club-firing/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Senior Discount Wednesday at Inner Light Crystals
