BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:13th Annual Post-Thanksgiving Turkey Waddle Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T123000
UID:261029CO7XjxeMDU6_D3eJnZP0QQ
DESCRIPTION:Jack London State Historic Park’s annual Turkey Waddle Hike 
 lets everyone get out and “shake their tail feathers” after a day of f
 easting and football.   Celebrated on the day after Thanksgiving since 2
 014\, this moderate 3.5-mile round trip hike leads through mixed evergreen
 s on the way to the majestic Ancient Redwood (also affectionately known as
  the Grandmother Tree).\n\n Great for all ages\, “waddlers” should we
 ar sturdy shoes and bring water.  The trail includes uneven and rocky sur
 faces and involves some elevation gain and loss.  The event will be cance
 lled in the event of rain. \n\n Tickets are $15 per person (the park ent
 ry fee is waived).   Reservations and more information are available at 
 https://jacklondonpark.com/events/turkey-waddle-2026/.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/turkey-waddle-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
