BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T170000
UID:261004R4aLy2FoDkyzbxKwT5zvlA
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Antarctica: The Frozen Desert | Photographs by Vegar Abelsnes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T170000
UID:260914anh7tIC7EUSLotLMp22RPQ
DESCRIPTION:1st Street Gallery at WTRSHD will present *“Antarctica: The 
 Frozen Desert\,”* a new body of fine art photography by Vegar Abelsnes\,
  opening September 26th\, 2026\, and on view September through November. 
  The exhibition marks a deliberate turn in Abelsnes’ photography\; after
  more than two decades of working in a commercial and advertising capacity
 \, he has embarked on a career as a photo and field guide in the polar reg
 ions. The exhibit features work generated over 6 *voyages to the* Antarcti
 c Peninsula. He is returning to Antarctica in January and will add the Fal
 klands and South Georgia to his list of destinations to guide and photogra
 ph.\n\nTraveling to some of the most remote and inhospitable coastlines on
  Earth\, Abelsnes has photographed a landscape that exists almost entirely
  outside of human time. The ice in these images began forming millions of 
 years ago\, while Homo sapiens have only existed for roughly 300\,000 year
 s. Defined by such a scale\, Antarctica is less a place than a record — 
 vast\, indifferent\, treacherous\, and staggeringly beautiful\, holding a 
 kind of cosmic truth that Abelsnes says is more important now than ever be
 fore.
LOCATION:1st Street Gallery @ WTRSHD
URL:https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Moonalice
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T200000
UID:261031UkidmnnDME2vRc6dbWBf5A
DESCRIPTION:Moonalice is a psychedelic\, roots-rock band of seasoned music
 ians mixing a variety of genres with extended musical improvisations that 
 evoke a sense of adventure and exploration. Everyone is a part of the expe
 rience and the music inspires dancing and other acts of self expression. E
 very show has an original art poster created by a well-known artist memori
 alizing that event and given to all attendees…each poster has its own Mo
 onalice legend. All concerts are broadcasted live in HD and available in a
 rchive shortly after their set.\n\nMoonalice plays mostly original materia
 l mixed with several covers\, and during their extended freeform jams the 
 band moves as one\, drawing from many musical genres honed from years of e
 xperience playing with various major acts. Their single "It's 4:20 Somewhe
 re" has been downloaded over 6 million times. Just released: 420 Gathering
  of the Tribe by Jay Blakesberg and Alex Fischer – a short film about th
 e Moonalice posters and poster artists: http://www.moonalice.com/song/its-
 420-somewhere. Social media: nearly 424\,000 on Facebook & over 67\,000 on
  Twitter. Their extensive tour schedule and videos of every Moonalice show
  can be seen at moonalice.com and every show poster with legends can be vi
 ewed at moonaliceposters.com.\n\nBand\n\nDylan Chambers: Vocals\, Cowbell 
 \\(Midnight Transit\, The New Chambers Brothers\\)\n\nLester Chambers: Voc
 als\, Harmonica \\(Chambers Brothers\, The New Chambers Brothers\\)\n\nJas
 on Crosby: Keyboards \\(Phil Lesh\, Terrapin Family Band\, Jenny Lewis\, J
 ohn McLaughlin\, Robert Randolph\, Blind Boys of Alabama\, Susan Tedeschi\
 \)\n\nRoger McNamee: Rhythm Guitar\, Vocals\, Bass. \\(Guff\, The Engineer
 s\, Random Axes\, Flying Other Brothers\\)\n\nJohn Molo: Drums\, Vocals. \
 \(Bruce Hornsby & The Range\, John Fogerty\, Phil Lesh & Friends\, The Oth
 er Ones\, David Nelson Band\\).\n\nPete Sears: Bass\, Keyboards\, Guitar\,
  Vocals \\(Sam Gopal Dream\, Rod Stewart\, Jefferson Starship\, Jerry Garc
 ia\, Hot Tuna\, John Lee Hooker\, David Nelson Band\, Phil Lesh & Friends\
 \).\n\nBarry Sless: Lead Guitar\, Pedal Steel Guitar\, Bass. \\(Phil Lesh 
 & Friends\, David Nelson Band\, Kingfish\, Cowboy Jazz\\).\n\nChloe Tietje
 n: Vocals \\(T Sisters\\)\n\nErika Tietjen: Vocals\, Guitar \\(T Sisters\\
 )\n\nRachel Tietjen: Vocals\, Guitar \\(T Sisters\\)\n\nFun facts\n\nMoona
 lice’s first show was in May\, 2007.\n\nMoonalice’s single\, “It’s
  4:20 Somewhere” has been downloaded more than 5 million times.\n\nMoona
 lice invented the Twittercast concert\, broadcasting links in near real ti
 me for live concerts and at random times for past shows. The band has done
  103 Twittercast concerts.\n\nMoonalice is the first band to Mooncast live
  video of all of its concerts. Moonalice has broadcast nearly ever concert
  since 2010\, the first band to operate a satellite-based broadcast system
  that enables High Definition live video to smartphones and iPads WITHOUT 
 an app!
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1040623210?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rock Talk at Inner Light Crystals
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T130000
UID:2610277Rb4rMicskS0HeWqbP-4hA
DESCRIPTION:Join us Saturdays at Inner Light Crystals for Rock Talk - a fr
 ee weekly exploration of rocks\, minerals\, crystals\, geology\, and the f
 ascinating things the Earth creates.\n\nEach week we explore something a l
 ittle different\, from mineral families and formations to unusual specimen
 s\, geological processes\, and the details that make rocks and minerals so
  interesting.\n\nCome curious. Bring your questions. Geek out with us.\n\n
 Rock Talk begins at 12 PM and typically runs approximately 30–60 minutes
 .\n\nFREE to attend.\n\nInner Light Crystals\n\n4936 Sonoma Hwy\n\nSanta R
 osa\, CA\n\nSaturdays at Noon
LOCATION:Inner Light Crystals
URL:http://www.innerlightcrystalshop.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New Moon Circus Presents ‘La Lune Brille’
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T173000
UID:261023m2EaIDZ7xUqaCmGj2PUxkQ
DESCRIPTION:**New Moon Circus Presents ‘La Lune Brille’: a highly orig
 inal\, all-human circus that enchants through breathtaking acrobatics and 
 athletically stunning skill.**\n\n**Sonoma\, CA— November 27 - Dec 27 
 –** This 2026 winter season\, New Moon Circus invites audiences to ‘La
  Lune Brille’ — memorable family fun and stunning artistry under the i
 ntimate and charming atmosphere of the ‘petite’ big top.\n\nMeet the W
 inter moon and her frenemy\, the Sun.  When the moon is pushed from the s
 ky\, she must find a way home to the stars. Come along the journey as she 
 encounters mysterious beings and friendly creatures on the way.\n\nA child
  pleasing origin myth told through impressive aerialists\, jugglers\, acro
 bats\, and clever comedy\, this show blends classic storybook atmosphere w
 ith celestial magic. La Lune Brille will surprise\, dazzle and delight all
  ages.\n\nSpectators for all showings are invited to the European style ci
 rcus tent to experience the magic up to 30 minutes before each show. Corne
 rstone Sonoma will provide light concession and libations for purchase. \
 n\nThe event will include a 15 minute intermission during the 1 and a half
  hour show.\n\nLimited free parking is available at the location at Corner
 stone Sonoma.\n\nTickets for La Lune Brille are now available for purchase
  online at thenewmooncircus.com.\n\nIndividual ticket prices start at $40.
  Front row (VIP)\, options start at $65. Find showtimes and more details a
 t thenewmooncircus.com. Early booking is encouraged for this highly antici
 pated event.
LOCATION:CORNERSTONE SONOMA - Under the Big Top Tent  
URL:https://newmooncircus.ticketspice.com/new-moon-circus
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
