BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Salsa Intermediate with Steven Khuong (6 Weeks)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T191500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T201500
UID:261019OK1AL84aDE68qxne7g3Mqw
DESCRIPTION:**December 2 – January 6 (6 weeks)**\n\n**7:15 PM – 8:15 P
 M 4140 Redwood Highway #8\, San Rafael\, CA**\n\nReady to take your salsa 
 to the next level? This 6-week salsa intermediate Marin series is designed
  for dancers who already know the basics (timing\, basic steps\, and simpl
 e turns\, etc.) and want to build the confidence and versatility to shine 
 on the social dance floor.\n\n**In this class\, you’ll:**\n\nDevelop ada
 ptability so you can flow with different partners and music.\n\nRefine you
 r footwork and styling for sharper expression.\n\nMaster more complex turn
  patterns and combinations.\n\nStrengthen your lead and follow for smoothe
 r\, more connected dancing.\n\n**What to Expect:** Steven’s teaching sty
 le blends structure with fun\, creating a supportive space where you’ll 
 be challenged but never overwhelmed. Each week builds on the last\, helpin
 g you progress steadily while keeping the joy of salsa front and center.\n
 \n**Details:**\n\nNo partner necessary — rotations ensure everyone gets 
 to dance.\n\nPlease wear **non-marking shoe soles** to protect the floor
 .\n\nArrive 10 minutes early to warm up and get settled.\n\nDate & Time: W
 ednesdays @ 7:15PM – 8:15PM\n\nInstructor: Steven Khuong\n\nAddress: 414
 0 Redwood Highway #8 San Rafael\, CA
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin 
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/intermediate-salsa-wednesday-715-pm/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bottega Cellar Series with Stony Hill Vineyard & Heitz Cellar
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T210000
UID:261006MWcbkzgXCUK0WgX5FtfezA
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Bottega on December 2nd for an elegant evening feat
 uring Stony Hill Vineyard and Heitz Cellar\, hosted by Carlton McCoy Jr.\,
  Master Sommelier and CEO of Lawrence Wine Estates. Lawrence Wine Estates'
  Stony Hill Vineyard and Heitz Cellar are two of Napa Valley's most storie
 d wineries. Founded on Spring Mountain in 1952 by the McCrea family\, Ston
 y Hill built its legacy on high-elevation Chardonnay and Riesling\, becomi
 ng known as one of America's great white wine producers. Heitz Cellar\, fo
 unded in 1961 by Joe and Alice Heitz\, pioneered single-vineyard designate
 d wines with Napa's first vineyard-designated Cabernet Sauvignon\, helping
  establish the very idea of site-specific terroir in the valley. Hosted by
  the dynamic Carlton McCoy\, Master Sommelier and CEO of Lawrence Wine Est
 ates. Guests will experience a thoughtfully curated progression of wines h
 ighlighting two of Napa Valley’s most distinctive wineries\, moving from
  expressive Chardonnay to a remarkable selection of Cabernet Sauvignon fro
 m Spring Mountain\, Rutherford\, and Oakville. The wines will be paired wi
 th a seasonal multi-course menu by Bottega Executive Chef Alex Espinoza\, 
